# Copy to .env for LOCAL stats generation (never commit .env — it's gitignored).
# In production these come from GitHub Actions secrets, not this file.

# Use a READ-ONLY, FINE-GRAINED PAT:
#   Repository access:      All repositories
#   Repository permissions: Contents -> Read-only, Metadata -> Read-only
# Give it an expiry and rotate it. A read-only token can only READ repos (incl.
# private code) — it cannot push, delete, or change settings, so a leak has a
# small blast radius.
#
# A classic token with `repo` + `read:user` also works, but `repo` grants
# read + WRITE to every one of your repos — NOT recommended for this.
GH_TOKEN=github_pat_your_token_here

# Your GitHub username
GH_USER=isumitjha
